            <ArticleTitle>An open trial of zimelidine in patients with endogenous depression.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>13 patients with endogenous depression, who had failed to obtain a lasting response to other antidepressant drugs or to electroconvulsive therapy, were treated with zimelidine. 3 showed a marked, and 3 a mild improvement. Side effects were minimal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
